  "investigation_notes": "Uploads failure investigation - `insufficient_evidence`\n\n**What was observed:**\n\n- App container `incidentlab-app-1` is `running` `Up 4 seconds` and DB container `incidentlab-db-1` is `running` `Up 9 seconds (healthy)` (E1).\n- Re-check via inspect: app `running: true, exit_code: 0, oom_killed: false` (E6), db `running: true, exit_code: 0, oom_killed: false, health: healthy` (E7).\n- App `/health` returns `503 {\"status\":\"unhealthy\"}` (E2) and still `503` on re-check (E12). Unhealthy is a symptom, not root cause.\n- Recent Docker events (E3) show both containers were destroyed/re-created and restarted at `2026-10-29T15:54:58Z` and again at `15:55:30Z`, with `incidentlab-db-1` returning to `health_status: healthy` via `pg_isready -U lab -d lab` after each start.\n\n**What was ruled out with evidence:**\n\n- Host storage full for uploads volume ruled out: `/srv/lab-data` `use_percent: 9.0`, `inode_use_percent: 0.2`, `available_mb: 410.6` (E8).\n- Root filesystem full ruled out: `/` `use_percent: 6.8`, `inode_use_percent: 1.5` (E11).\n- DB container down ruled out as current state: `healthy` (E7) and `Up 9 seconds (healthy)` (E1). App and DB share network `incidentlab_default` (E6, E7).\n- App crash/OOM at inspect time ruled out: `running: true, oom_killed: false` (E6).\n\n**What could not be determined - missing evidence:**\n\n- Application logs unavailable (E4) and database logs unavailable (E5) - `this data source is unavailable` - so the application error causing `503` (E2, E12) and upload failure cannot be seen.\n- Upload directory writability unknown: `path_access` for `/srv/lab-data/uploads` unavailable (E9) and for `/srv/lab-data` unavailable (E10). Cannot confirm or rule out permission / ownership problem despite knowing app runs as `1000:1000` with bind mount `source: /srv/lab-data -> destination: /data, rw: true` (E6).\n- No app healthcheck defined: `health: no healthcheck` (E6), so Docker health cannot corroborate (E2, E12).\n\n**Conclusion:**\n\n12/12 checks used. Because the key discriminating sources - logs (E4, E5) and path permission checks (E9, E10) - were unavailable, and disk (E8, E11) and running state (E1, E6, E7) alone do not show the cause itself, the outcome is `insufficient_evidence`. Do not repair based on assumption; need log access and manual `ls -ld /srv/lab-data/uploads` + write test as `uid 1000` and DB connectivity check from app.\n",
